{"name":"Sepia Filter","hex":"#cbb499","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sepia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brown pigment made from the secretions of the cuttlefish. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A dark, slightly reddish, brown colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sepia"},{"term":"filter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A device which separates a suspended, dissolved, or particulate matter from a fluid, solution, or other substance; any device that separates one substance from another.","Electronics or software that separates unwanted signals (for example noise) from wanted signals or that attenuates selected frequencies."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sort, sift, or isolate.","To diffuse; to cause to be less concentrated or focused."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/filter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sepia (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sepia is a reddish-brown color, named after the rich brown pigment derived from the ink sac of the common cuttlefish Sepia. The word sepia is the Latinized form of the Ancient Greek word σηπία, meaning cuttlefish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Codex_Atlanticus_-_000V-26.jpg/330px-Codex_Atlanticus_-_000V-26.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sepia_(color)"},{"title":"Filter (social media)","blocks":[{"text":"Filters are digital image effects often used on social media. They initially simulated the effects of camera filters, and they have since developed with facial recognition technology and computer-generated augmented reality. Social media filters—especially beauty filters—are often used to alter the appearance of selfies taken on smartphones or other similar devices. While filters are commonly associated with beauty enhancement and feature alterations, there is a wide range of filters that have different functions. From adjusting photo tones to using face animations and interactive elements, users have access to a range of tools. These filters allow users to enhance photos and allow room for creative expression and fun interactions with digital content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/A_selfie_taken_by_a_man_using_an_%22I_love_Wikipedia%22_filter.jpg/330px-A_selfie_taken_by_a_man_using_an_%22I_love_Wikipedia%22_filter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filter_(social_media)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Purikura_8jo_WATANABE_Hachijo.jpg/500px-Purikura_8jo_WATANABE_Hachijo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Purikura_8jo_WATANABE_Hachijo.jpg/500px-Purikura_8jo_WATANABE_Hachijo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photo sticker with beauty filter and various effects from a Purikura machine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APurikura_8jo_WATANABE_Hachijo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Instagram_Filters_2011.jpg/500px-Instagram_Filters_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Instagram_Filters_2011.jpg/1280px-Instagram_Filters_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Instagram_Filters_2011.jpg/500px-Instagram_Filters_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A photo collage of an original, unprocessed image (top left) modified with the 16 different filters available on Instagram in 2011","lin